{"title":"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two men at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d5db6ea360f9b1367e4db85c18474906401e2c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$76$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> miles apart, set out at the same time to walk towards each other. \nThe man at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> walks uniformly at the rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2333460a1b72d6b0ca58b9bbcee8820bc22672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\tfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"18\" height=\"21\" /> miles per hour; the man at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> walks at the constant \nrate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1e64ebec3c0b7fec0ca9f4b2596ac08ce37f311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\tfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"18\" height=\"21\" /> miles per hour for the first hour, at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e5c19bb07f1809abe0f1bfb175d4f9c74b06d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\tfrac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"18\" height=\"21\" /> miles per hour for the second hour,\nand so on, in arithmetic progression. If the men meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> miles nearer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> in an integral number of hours, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00d9b6525976c0629568375daf486ca59fbed7b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, find the number of hours it takes for the two to meet together.  After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> hours, the person at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> walks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb65fd6dde65947a231fab8613e08db5507eea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.5h$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> miles.  In the same amount of time, the person at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> has been walking at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a530bff97cb002dbd45bbb28ee8e1a01f3735ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.25+0.5(h-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" /> mph for the past hour, so the person walks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f1e9cdbaac1085d7e135d0e6ae322142d0e41da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h(6.5+0.5(h-1))}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"151\" height=\"38\" /> miles.\n</p><p>In order for both to meet, the sum of both of the distances walked must total <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d5db6ea360f9b1367e4db85c18474906401e2c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$76$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> miles, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2be2690f1bffed7041fe017b36691cc5132ff237.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4.5h + \\frac{h(6+0.5h)}{2} = 76\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547bb088d4e5fd17b5c9725ba1b28c2650af584f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4.5h + 3h + 0.25h^2 = 76\\]\" width=\"189\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12de1ddfa23df70e23edcab52a1d65050dc104f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.25h^2 + 7.5h - 76 = 0\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/9/5790bd43b20086fa9ec08cb46bd69022a51ad41f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h^2 + 30h - 304 = 0\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a1561aa1190d465edb28a3582ad0b777dfbe82fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(h + 38)(h - 8) = 0\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> must be positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51272d12a0553839d968213794875ac5ec41851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.  Because it takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours to meet, the person from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles while the person from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles.  Thus, they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME\" title=\"1963 AHSME\">1963 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1963 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1963\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a 